Package: rhodep-phosh-wifi-guard
Version: 1
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: rhodep port
Description: Keep Phosh alive across WiFi-auditing network churn on Motorola rhodep
 `airmon-ng check kill` stops NetworkManager/wpa_supplicant to free the radio for
 monitor mode. On this Phosh phone port that churn can stop phosh.service, and
 phoc (the Wayland compositor) then takes >90s to tear down, so systemd SIGKILLs
 it and OnFailure drops to a getty -> permanent black screen.
 .
 This package ships two reversible protections:
  - a phosh.service drop-in (Restart=always, RestartSec=3s, TimeoutStopSec=15s,
    StartLimitIntervalSec=0, empty OnFailure) so Phosh always comes back within
    a few seconds instead of latching failed or falling to getty; and
  - /usr/local/sbin/airmon-safe, a wrapper that does the "check kill" while
    explicitly shielding the phoc/phosh tree and restoring the network on exit.
 .
 Use `airmon-safe start wlanN` instead of `airmon-ng check kill`. Even the raw
 command no longer leaves a permanent black screen once the drop-in is in place.
 Note: the unrelated `ath10k ... chan info: invalid frequency 0 (idx 41 out of
 bounds)` kernel message is a cosmetic WCN3990 firmware quirk, not this issue.
